<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61399" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κώρῠκος</span></b> , ὁ,
			<u>Corycus</u>, a promontory of Cilicia, <i><span class="en">
			<u>h.Ap.</u>
			39
		</span></i>, etc.:— Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κωρυκαῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>: the inhabitants were
		infamous for <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spying out</i>
			the destination and value of ships' cargoes and then piratically
			seizing them, <i><span class="en">
				Ephor.
				27
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, etc.: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κωρυκαῖος</span>,
			prov. of <i>spies</i> and <i>eavesdroppers</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				14.1.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				10.18.1
			</span></i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Iamb.</u>
				1.143
			</span></i>; K. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠκροάσατο</span>, 'a little
			bird told me', <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				150
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ κατακούσειεν δέ μου
			ὁ</span> K., 'low be it spoken', <i><span class="en">
				Diox.
				2
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κωρύκιον</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάφος</span>
			<i>piratical</i> craft, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.8
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
